The invoice was not delivered. The tracking report shows the message is still deferred and queued for retry, with the last update 71 hours ago. Nothing in the output confirms that it reached l.steiner@steiner-holz.de, so the intended effect (the customer receiving the invoice) hasn't happened yet.

The message content looks right: the invoice number, amount, attachment, and due date (2026-10-23 plus 45 days is 2026-12-07) are all consistent. One thing to check is that the payment link points to pay.nordwerk-gmbh.at, a different domain from the customer's address, so confirm that domain is the expected one for payments. I haven't checked this against the runbook, and it doesn't change the delivery outcome.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.93, "reason": "The tracking shows the message is still deferred and queued for retry with no confirmed delivery to the billing contact."}

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.93}

The invoice reached the customer, but it was issued for the wrong amount. The work item specifies € 4,234.48. The sent email subject, the attached-invoice payment link, and the ledger entry for INV-2026-1967 all show € 423.45. The customer was billed a tenth of the correct amount, so the intended effect was not achieved.

The rest matches: the email was accepted by mx1.huber-bau.at and delivered to e.steiner@huber-bau.at, the PDF is attached, the CRM logs the send to K-93, and the due date of 2026-11-06 is correct for 14 days from 2026-10-23. The agent's "all checks green" report missed the amount mismatch, and the invoice has already been sent to the customer, so it needs correcting.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.93, "reason": "The invoice was delivered to the correct contact but for € 423.45 instead of the required € 4,234.48, so the billed amount is wrong."}

Only 91 duplicates were removed, but the runbook says the raw file has 368 duplicate respondents. Removing 368 would have left 16,841 rows, but the output has 17,118. Deduplication was incomplete, so 277 duplicates are still in the data.

The output reports 17,118 unique respondent_ids. That means the remaining duplicates are not identical on respondent_id, for example re-interviews recorded under a different id. The validation check only compares the row count against the 91 the job removed, so it didn't catch this.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.85, "reason": "Only 91 of the 368 known duplicate respondents were removed (17,118 rows remain instead of about 16,841), so deduplication is incomplete despite the green checks."}

The invoice did not reach the intended billing contact. The work item names e.huber@berger-moebel.de, but the SMTP log, delivery tracking, and CRM entry all show it was sent to a.berger@berger-moebel.de and accepted into that mailbox.

The other parts check out: the amount (€ 1,517.57), the attachment (invoice_INV-2026-1441.pdf), and the due date (2026-12-07, which is 45 days after 2026-10-23) all match. The CRM activity and the dunning reminder were also recorded against the wrong address, so the ledger now shows the customer as invoiced through a contact who is not the billing contact.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.9, "reason": "The invoice was delivered to a.berger@berger-moebel.de instead of the specified billing contact e.huber@berger-moebel.de, so the intended recipient never received it."}

The invoice was sent and delivered. The SMTP log shows the message from billing@nordwerk-gmbh.at to a.berger@berger-moebel.de, with subject "Invoice INV-2026-1441 (€ 1,517.57, due 2026-12-07)" and invoice_INV-2026-1441.pdf attached. The server accepted it at 10:49:14. Delivery tracking confirms delivery to that mailbox (DSN 2.0.0). The ledger shows INV-2026-1441 posted to customer K-17 for € 1,517.57 with status SENT, and the CRM logs an "invoice sent" activity on K-17 to the same address. The archive holds a 3-page PDF.

I did not see the invoice date of 2026-10-23 in any output, and I did not check that a.berger@berger-moebel.de is the correct contact for K-17 beyond the CRM record. Those are the remaining gaps, so my confidence is good but not complete.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.85, "reason": "SMTP, delivery tracking, ledger and CRM all confirm the correct invoice, amount, customer K-17 and PDF were sent and delivered to a.berger@berger-moebel.de, though the invoice date and the recipient's correctness were not independently verified."}

The invoice appears to have reached the customer. The receivables entry matches the work item on invoice number, customer K-83, and amount (€8,667.22), and shows status SENT. The CRM has an 'invoice sent' activity on K-83 that records the recipient address and the attached invoice_INV-2026-1741.pdf. The archive copy and the dunning reminder for 2026-11-13 are consistent with a sent invoice.

Two things keep my confidence below certainty. The "duplicate contact merge suggested for K-83" entry means the customer's contact record may be ambiguous, so I can't confirm from these logs that j.gruber@lindner-logistik.at is the correct billing contact. I also didn't check the runbook for the due-date convention, though 2026-11-06 is 14 days after the invoice date and looks plausible.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.85, "reason": "The receivables entry (K-83, €8,667.22, SENT), the CRM 'invoice sent' activity with the PDF attached, and the archive record all confirm the invoice was delivered to the customer, though the pending duplicate-contact merge leaves the recipient address slightly uncertain."}

The invoice appears to have reached the customer. The receivables entry shows INV-2026-1741 posted to K-83 for €8,667.22, matching the work item, with status SENT and a due date of 2026-11-06. The CRM log has an 'invoice sent' activity on K-83 addressed to j.gruber@lindner-logistik.at, with invoice_INV-2026-1741.pdf attached (85 kB). The archive holds the 3-page PDF, and a dunning reminder is scheduled for 2026-11-13.

The rest of the output concerns other invoices and customers, so it doesn't bear on this one. The open item is the "duplicate contact merge suggested for K-83." It doesn't affect the send that already happened, but someone should review it so the K-83 record and its contact are not changed without checking. I didn't check the runbook for conventions on due dates or dunning timing, so the agent's "all checks green" is supported by the system entries rather than independently verified against those rules.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.85, "reason": "Receivables shows INV-2026-1741 posted to K-83 for €8,667.22 with status SENT, and CRM logs an 'invoice sent' activity to the customer's address with the PDF attached."}

The invoice reached the customer. The mail log shows the message from billing@nordwerk-gmbh.at to j.gruber@lindner-logistik.at, with invoice_INV-2026-1741.pdf attached, accepted by the recipient's server at 10:58:33 after one greylist retry. The delivery report confirms delivery to that mailbox. The ledger shows INV-2026-1741 posted to K-83 for € 8,667.22 with status SENT, and the CRM logs an "invoice sent" activity on K-83 with the same recipient and attachment. The PDF was archived and a dunning reminder is scheduled for 2026-11-13, which is consistent with a sent invoice.

Two small caveats: I could not independently confirm that j.gruber is the correct contact for K-83, since the only evidence is the CRM record that the invoice was sent to that address. The CRM also suggests a duplicate contact merge for K-83, which is worth a look but does not show the send failed.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.85, "reason": "The invoice was accepted by the recipient mailbox with the correct PDF and amount, and the ledger and CRM both record INV-2026-1741 as sent to K-83."}

